{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/265384-demons-and-twilight","id":265384,"title":"Demons and Twilight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-25T06:07:46-07:00","id":265384,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Demons and Twilight","content":"So I've read over all the existing Demon material and one thing that I'm still unclear on is how Demons can interact with things in Twilight. Given that Angels exist mostly in Twilight it seems like it would be increaidbly useful to be able to see and/or interact with Twilight but I can't recall a single power or form ability that allowed either. In fact given that their lack of souls means demons can't use abjurations or wards they seem to be in fact less equipped to deal with Twilight entities than normal humans.<br /> <br /> The only exception I know of is Ephemeral cover but that presents its own issues in that the demon needs to be able to find ghosts or spirits to use it and given that they can't see them this seems a pretty hard task.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something or do people have ideas of how to deal with this or am I looking at it wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T07:25:06-07:00","id":265439,"title":"","content":"Abjuration is used by mortals to tear down the conditions that an entity uses to maintain its connection to the world. Without those conditions they bleed essence. Unlike most mortals, a demon has the ability to see and perceive infrastructure immediately. So while no more equipped to perceive twilight than a mortal they <i>are</i> automatically equipped to target the necessary infrastructure that angels need to survive. Seeking the linchpin of an infrastructure and disrupting it or destroying it in some way will remove that condition, and hopefully collapse the reliant conditions also. Any angels immediately start to bleed essence and when they reach zero they go dormant; defeating them.<br /> <br /> The &quot;sense the angelic&quot; modification also helps a demon positively identify in a single check an area where angelic numina have been used in the past 24 hours and identify an individual currently under the affects of angelic numina.<br /> <br /> The &quot;essence drain&quot; technology also helps a demon combat ephemeral creatures by stealing their essence and converting it into aether.<br /> <br /> The &quot;reality reinforcement&quot; exploit is hugely powerful for dealing with non-manifest angels, as it forces them to materialise <i>and </i>locks out their numina.<br /> <br /> A demon could also make a gadget out of any of the above powers (and also ephemeral cover) to hypothetically both affect and see into twilight. (Though this trick would require storyteller permission).<br /> <br /> I am, however, struggling to find anything that suggests a demon <i>couldn't</i> use warding and abjuration. Boltholes can have warding, so a demon has to be able to do that somehow, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T11:58:58-07:00","id":265613,"title":"","content":"I think that Ramza's assertion that a Demon cannot use abjuration is based off the Demon's lack of an Integrity stat and the effects of the Soulless condition. The Soulless condition explicitly prevents abjuration, warding, and binding. Demons don't have souls, but they don't have the Soulless condition. Whether that still prevents abjuration seems like a judgment call for the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> My personal interpretation would be that a Demon in Cover can use abjuration with the Cover acting as a kind of pseudo-soul in place of Integrity. Otherwise, there's no way for a Demon to repair their own wards if the wards on their bolthole are breached.<br /> <br /> ETA - Also, if a Demon can't use abjuration, then it creates a kind of Demon test that can't be beaten by spoofing, which seems like a bad precedent to set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 09-25-2014, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T07:19:40-07:00","id":266138,"title":"","content":"I would say there is some implication that your interpretation could be true and I, personally, would be inclined to agree with you. Soul Pacts, for example, aren't for the mortal's soul, but for their place in the universe. But, never the less, you buy their life, and existence, and have to shunt their soul out to do it. This would suggest to me that a Cover is sort of made from &quot;Soul Stuff&quot; perhaps? While not a soul itself, it certainly tricks the universe into thinking that it's one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:48:33-07:00","id":266556,"title":"","content":"I figured that the Demon in using a Cover is essentially 'wearing a soul'... The Demon does not have one as is, but through the Covers they can make use of them (or perhaps the Cover is merely spoofing a Soul?). Of course this gets into the debate of a piece of Patchwork Cover having 'Soul'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}